<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BPA boosted Q1 profit 905 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BPA boosted Q1 profit 905 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ending March 31.</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net profit			 4.5    vs	0.45</p>
<p>Total assets			3,748.0    vs  2,726.00</p>
<p>Client loans			  775.0    vs    903.00</p>
<p>Total client funds		1,874.0    vs  1,791.00</p>
<p>Unpaid loans over 90 days    4.5 percent vs    4.9 percent</p>
<p>ROA				  0,5 percent vs    0.1 percent</p>
<p>ROE				 13.6 percent vs    1.5 percent</p>
<p>Note - Banco Portugues do Atlantico is controlled 50 percent Banco Comercial Portugues with nearly 48 percent held by insurer Imperio.</p>
<p>The positive result was achieved by reductions in costs, reduced provisions against risky loans and the sale of non-strategic holdings, BCP chairman Jorge Jardim Goncalves told journalists.</p>
<p>Staff costs fell 13.4 percent compared with the same quarter last year. The volume of overdue loans fell 14 billion escudos over the period.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
